WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.400
-You are a stud.
Come on, we love you.

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.567
-Look at you.
-I love you.

00:00:03.567 --> 00:00:06.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Oh, thank you.

00:00:06.267 --> 00:00:10.300
-I look like a bad Spirit
Halloween costume of you.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.033
-Looks like we're going
as each other for Halloween.

00:00:12.033 --> 00:00:14.534
-[ Laughs ]
Welcome back to the show.

00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:15.801
I have a lot of things
to talk to you about.

00:00:15.801 --> 00:00:16.834
-Sure.

00:00:16.834 --> 00:00:17.934
-I want to talk about
"Spirited."

00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:19.801
I want to talk about
Will Ferrell.

00:00:19.801 --> 00:00:23.467
I want to talk about -- can we
talk about baby number four?

00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:26.234
-Oh, boy. Let's get into it,
Barbara Walters.

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:27.734
Let's do this.
-You know me.

00:00:27.734 --> 00:00:29.434
-Let's do this.
-Congratulations.

00:00:29.434 --> 00:00:31.334
-Thank you.
-Baby number four on the way.

00:00:31.334 --> 00:00:32.968
Number four.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:32.968 --> 00:00:34.667
♪♪

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:37.267
I'm so happy for you and Blake.
-Thank you.

00:00:37.267 --> 00:00:40.000
-Send my best to Blake, please.
-I definitely will.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.534
Yeah, it's another --
it's a lot.

00:00:42.534 --> 00:00:45.067
I mean, we have three
beautiful girls right now

00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:47.067
and fourth one on the way.

00:00:47.067 --> 00:00:50.300
It's really
making me rethink stunts.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:53.200
You know, I've been doing
action movies for 25 years.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:54.567
I've broken 12 bones.

00:00:54.567 --> 00:00:56.667
I just had a seventh surgery.

00:00:56.667 --> 00:00:59.167
And, you know, kids, though,
they beat you up.

00:00:59.167 --> 00:01:01.701
I got, you know, my daughter's
like, you know, you --

00:01:01.701 --> 00:01:04.567
I oftentimes -- like, it's not
an alarm clock that wakes me up.

00:01:04.567 --> 00:01:06.934
It's like a knee to the jugular.
-Yeah, of course.

00:01:06.934 --> 00:01:08.067
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:09.834
And I just want to keep --

00:01:09.834 --> 00:01:12.334
I'm rethinking doing stunts now
because I'm starting to realize,

00:01:12.334 --> 00:01:14.267
like, I want to be able
to still kind of be active

00:01:14.267 --> 00:01:15.400
with my kids and stuff.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:18.234
Like, I love throwing them
up in the air.

00:01:18.234 --> 00:01:20.501
Like, I can throw my daughter
Betty, especially --

00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:21.868
I can throw her --
she's so little,

00:01:21.868 --> 00:01:24.067
I can throw her high in the air.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.067 --> 00:01:26.033
-Yeah.
-Still, and she loves it.

00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:28.334
The problem is,
I can't catch her...

00:01:28.334 --> 00:01:30.100
-Yeah.
That's how they learn.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:34.234
-...any more, so that's the
biggest issue that I'm facing.

00:01:34.234 --> 00:01:35.701
But, yeah.

00:01:35.701 --> 00:01:37.634
-Do you know
if it's a boy or a girl?

00:01:37.634 --> 00:01:38.767
-We don't.
We never find out.

00:01:38.767 --> 00:01:41.701
We always wait till they
come down the chute.

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.067
But, you know, I actually, um...

00:01:43.067 --> 00:01:44.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.901 --> 00:01:46.267
-Your doctor said that?
-Yeah.

00:01:46.267 --> 00:01:48.667
I just --
Even after they're born,

00:01:48.667 --> 00:01:50.434
I don't ask
'cause I respect their privacy.

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:52.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:55.434
But I'm kind of hoping
for a girl 'cause I know

00:01:55.434 --> 00:01:57.901
I'm a bit of a hen myself.
I know girls.

00:01:57.901 --> 00:02:00.133
I like -- I'm a girl dad.
I'm used to that.

00:02:00.133 --> 00:02:02.334
I'm ready for that.
I feel like --

00:02:02.334 --> 00:02:03.701
[ Cheers and applause ]
Right, yeah?

00:02:03.701 --> 00:02:06.501
-Yeah, you're a good dad.
-I feel like, if, you know,

00:02:06.501 --> 00:02:09.467
like, history has taught us
anything, that one day --

00:02:09.467 --> 00:02:11.234
if we have a son,
that one day my life will be

00:02:11.234 --> 00:02:15.367
taken by that son, you know,
in some horrible way.

00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:17.067
If it's anything
like my childhood, he'll end up

00:02:17.067 --> 00:02:19.167
on the lawn with me
in a fistfight like my dad.

00:02:19.167 --> 00:02:21.601
-Yeah, Thanksgiving.
-Yeah.

00:02:21.601 --> 00:02:24.067
-I want to ask you
about this, too.

00:02:24.067 --> 00:02:26.534
You are an owner
of a professional soccer team.

00:02:26.534 --> 00:02:28.067
-Yes.
Wrexham AFC, yeah.

00:02:28.067 --> 00:02:30.000
-Wrexham AFC.
Congratulations on that, bud.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.834
-Me and Rob McElhenney.
But thank you.

00:02:31.834 --> 00:02:33.133
Thank you very much, yeah.
-Pretty big deal.

00:02:33.133 --> 00:02:34.801
-It is a big deal.
Yeah, we're -- I'm very excited.

00:02:34.801 --> 00:02:36.634
Yeah.
-How do you get into that?

00:02:36.634 --> 00:02:38.601
Do you know at all
what you're doing?

00:02:38.601 --> 00:02:39.734
-No. No, no, no.
God no.

00:02:39.734 --> 00:02:42.434
Um, nothing at all.
It's kind of absurd.

00:02:42.434 --> 00:02:43.801
But I do know about
storytelling.

00:02:43.801 --> 00:02:45.300
Most organizations,
they kind of grow

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:46.767
and they're built
on best practices.

00:02:46.767 --> 00:02:48.968
And I think that's overlooked
often about how important

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.400
storytelling is to sports.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.567
I mean, sports is driven
by emotion, right?

00:02:52.567 --> 00:02:55.400
So storytelling can grow
a sports club

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:58.400
in a really beautiful
and distinctly amazing way.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:00.934
So I love that about it.
Rob McElhenney and I both

00:03:00.934 --> 00:03:03.067
love everything about Wrexham
for that reason.

00:03:03.067 --> 00:03:04.968
-There's a rumor going around
that you may be interested

00:03:04.968 --> 00:03:08.000
in buying an NHL
professional hockey team,

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.234
the Ottawa Senators.
-The Ottawa Senators.

00:03:10.234 --> 00:03:11.701
Yes, that is true.
-It's a Canadian team.

00:03:11.701 --> 00:03:14.267
-Yeah. It's an NHL team,
the Ottawa Senators.

00:03:14.267 --> 00:03:17.901
I am trying to do --
It's a very expensive --

00:03:17.901 --> 00:03:20.634
So, you know, I need to be --
-It's not like something --

00:03:20.634 --> 00:03:23.467
-Yeah, I need a partner with,
you know, really deep pockets.

00:03:23.467 --> 00:03:25.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.868
It's called a --
It's called a consortium --

00:03:27.868 --> 00:03:30.000
"consorshum"
or a "con-sort-ium" --

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.767
when you form a group together
to buy an entity.

00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:34.868
And I -- it's such
a fancy way of saying,

00:03:34.868 --> 00:03:36.367
"I need a sugar mommy
or a sugar daddy."

00:03:36.367 --> 00:03:37.567
-Okay, yeah, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.567 --> 00:03:39.601
You do need one.
-Yeah, and if that doesn't

00:03:39.601 --> 00:03:41.267
work out,
I'll buy a U.S. senator,

00:03:41.267 --> 00:03:43.267
which anyone can afford.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:43.267 --> 00:03:45.934
You know.
That's kind of the --

00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:48.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's sort of key there.

00:03:48.167 --> 00:03:50.901
-Wait -- yeah.
Wait till Wednesday, yeah.

00:03:50.901 --> 00:03:53.200
-But I love Ottawa.
I grew up in Vancouver,

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:54.400
which has my heart always,

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.567
but I also grew up
in Ottawa, Canada.

00:03:56.567 --> 00:03:58.734
I spent a long time
in Vanier there,

00:03:58.734 --> 00:04:00.400
which is a little town
right inside Ottawa.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:04.267
-And hockey is just part of the
system when you grow up.

00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:06.000
That's part of your blood.
-It's sad, it's scary,

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.434
but children
are eased out of the womb

00:04:07.434 --> 00:04:08.834
in ice skates in Canada.

00:04:08.834 --> 00:04:10.000
I mean, that's how they're born.
-They really are.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:11.133
-They're ready to go, yeah.

00:04:11.133 --> 00:04:12.767
NHL-ready
by the time they're 4.

00:04:12.767 --> 00:04:15.067
-That's amazing, though.
But you could do that,

00:04:15.067 --> 00:04:17.400
and then you're running this --
that's the dream.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:20.200
-Wrexham has consumed
half of my life.

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:22.367
And then, the other half

00:04:22.367 --> 00:04:23.968
might be consumed
by something like this.

00:04:23.968 --> 00:04:26.167
I figure the kids, my kids,
they've got it now.

00:04:26.167 --> 00:04:27.901
They can do it on their own
from this point forward.

00:04:27.901 --> 00:04:29.300
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:31.033
-Yeah.
Now you're throwing them up

00:04:31.033 --> 00:04:32.801
and not catching them.
-Yeah.

00:04:32.801 --> 00:04:34.434
It's just a dad-sized hole
in the wall.

00:04:34.434 --> 00:04:36.400
I'm gone.
-You're gone.

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:38.200
-Like singing Reba McEntire.

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:40.534
♪ I'm a single mom
who works two jobs ♪

00:04:40.534 --> 00:04:41.701
-Wow!
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.701 --> 00:04:43.868
-♪ Who loves her kids
and never stops ♪

00:04:43.868 --> 00:04:46.200
-Hey, by the way,
you have a great voice.

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:47.267
-No, no, that's terrible.

00:04:47.267 --> 00:04:49.601
-No, no,
but the movie, "Spirited."

00:04:49.601 --> 00:04:51.767
Can I just say, I loved it.

00:04:51.767 --> 00:04:53.200
You're gonna freak out.

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:56.767
It is so funny,
and it's also a great musical.

00:04:56.767 --> 00:04:58.267
It's a good story to it.
-Yeah.

00:04:58.267 --> 00:04:59.834
Pasek and Paul
did all the music for it.

00:04:59.834 --> 00:05:02.100
They did "La La Land"
and "Greatest Showman."

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:04.234
Oh, my God, I mean --
"Dear Evan Hansen."

00:05:04.234 --> 00:05:06.968
I mean, tons of stuff.
-Speaking of "Greatest Showman,"

00:05:06.968 --> 00:05:09.634
Hugh Jackman --
hold your applause.

00:05:09.634 --> 00:05:10.834
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.834 --> 00:05:13.100
The -- He --

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:16.000
You are teaming up with Hugh
for "Deadpool 3."

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:18.000
-Yes. Yes, I am.
Very excited about that.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:20.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:20.234 --> 00:05:21.701
It's kind of amazing.
-I mean, that's --

00:05:21.701 --> 00:05:24.300
That would be -- that's so fun.
-Yeah.

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:27.467
-But Wolverine --
he's bringing Wolverine --

00:05:27.467 --> 00:05:30.667
-Bringing in Wolverine, yeah.
We figured out a way to do it

00:05:30.667 --> 00:05:32.968
that Hugh Jackman approved
and Kevin Feige approved,

00:05:32.968 --> 00:05:34.701
where we're completely
protecting the legacy

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:36.100
of "Logan,"
the way it was left off.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:37.501
We wouldn't mess with that.

00:05:37.501 --> 00:05:39.200
And I'm really excited about it.
As I've gotten

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:41.501
a little bit older,
I sort of want to --

00:05:41.501 --> 00:05:43.634
really, I'm lucky that I get
to work in this industry

00:05:43.634 --> 00:05:45.367
and particularly
incredibly fortunate

00:05:45.367 --> 00:05:46.601
that I get to work in it
this long.

00:05:46.601 --> 00:05:48.734
But I really want to work
with people I either --

00:05:48.734 --> 00:05:50.567
that are either
immensely talented

00:05:50.567 --> 00:05:54.534
or people that I love and I'm
genuinely best friends with.

00:05:54.534 --> 00:05:56.701
Unfortunately, Hugh does not
qualify as either of those.

00:05:56.701 --> 00:05:59.300
[ Laughter ]
But I am excited

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:01.734
'cause I'm a "Logan" fan.
So...

00:06:01.734 --> 00:06:04.434
And then, that covers
Will Ferrell, as well.

00:06:04.434 --> 00:06:06.234
That's a guy that I've --

00:06:06.234 --> 00:06:08.634
I mean, my entire life,
I feel,

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:10.601
I've ached
to work with Will Ferrell.

00:06:10.601 --> 00:06:12.033
-He's unbelievable, right?
Isn't he fun?

00:06:12.033 --> 00:06:13.734
-Oh, my God.
I don't know -- yeah.

00:06:13.734 --> 00:06:15.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:15.234 --> 00:06:18.300
-But you two, together...
-It's just like --

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:20.167
I don't know that you find
a comedic actor

00:06:20.167 --> 00:06:23.534
that has contributed more to
the modern comedy lexicon

00:06:23.534 --> 00:06:24.968
than Will Ferrell.

00:06:24.968 --> 00:06:26.634
I mean, people are doing
Will Ferrell --

00:06:26.634 --> 00:06:28.501
The hardest challenge
of "Spirited" wasn't just

00:06:28.501 --> 00:06:30.200
the singing and dancing
and all that other stuff,

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:32.801
it was to not do
an impression of Will Ferrell

00:06:32.801 --> 00:06:35.200
to [bleep] Will Ferrell.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:37.234
Like, that was the big --
that was the hardest thing.

00:06:37.234 --> 00:06:38.667
-Yeah, you're like,
"Oh, I delivered that line.

00:06:38.667 --> 00:06:41.667
Oh, I delivered it like you."
-"I just Elfed you.

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:42.968
Oh, God."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:42.968 --> 00:06:45.167
-"I just Elfed you," yeah.
-"So sorry, man."

00:06:45.167 --> 00:06:48.634
-Can we set up what "Spirited"
is about and who you play?

00:06:48.634 --> 00:06:50.300
The idea --
the premise is brilliant.

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:53.534
-Yeah, it's a modern take
on Charles Dickens,

00:06:53.534 --> 00:06:55.501
who's this hacky writer
that used to write some stuff.

00:06:55.501 --> 00:06:56.934
[ Laughter ]
-No, that's not true.

00:06:56.934 --> 00:07:00.901
-Called "A Christmas Carol."
And it is a more modern take.

00:07:00.901 --> 00:07:03.133
I play the -- Will plays the
Ghost of Christmas Present,

00:07:03.133 --> 00:07:05.067
and we actually are now
in his perspective,

00:07:05.067 --> 00:07:07.834
which has never been done with
this type of story before.

00:07:07.834 --> 00:07:09.534
So, we get to see this
from the ghost's perspective.

00:07:09.534 --> 00:07:12.300
But I play Clint Briggs.
I'm sort of this year's Scrooge.

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:15.200
And what makes me this year's
Scrooge is that I'm basically

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:18.334
one of these guys that uses
or hijacks social media

00:07:18.334 --> 00:07:20.234
and those kinds of things
to be divisive,

00:07:20.234 --> 00:07:22.234
to divide people
and continue to polarize people,

00:07:22.234 --> 00:07:24.100
which I think is actually
a great modern,

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:27.767
sort of perfectly apt
and well-timed horrible trait

00:07:27.767 --> 00:07:30.200
for this guy to have,
to make him Scrooge.

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:33.534
So, it's based -- and then
it's singing, dancing, I mean --

00:07:33.534 --> 00:07:35.734
-By the way,
who knew you could dance?

00:07:35.734 --> 00:07:37.467
-No one, and not me.
That's for sure.

00:07:37.467 --> 00:07:39.400
[ Laughter ]
-You were fantastic.

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:40.601
-I mean, it was --

00:07:40.601 --> 00:07:41.934
-How long
did you train for this?

00:07:41.934 --> 00:07:46.033
-We trained for -- Dance camp
was two months before.

00:07:46.033 --> 00:07:49.133
But we trained for three months
before that with Chloe Arnold,

00:07:49.133 --> 00:07:51.133
who's one of the greatest
tap dancers in the world,

00:07:51.133 --> 00:07:53.300
and Maud Arnold, her sister,
and I just --

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:55.133
You know, I basically
was aiming for, like,

00:07:55.133 --> 00:07:58.901
a black belt in adequate,
just to get through.

00:07:58.901 --> 00:08:00.834
-You want to be the best
at adequate.

00:08:00.834 --> 00:08:03.267
-Yeah, all I ever said --
all me and Will ever said

00:08:03.267 --> 00:08:05.667
to Chloe Arnold was just,
"Yes, ma'am."

00:08:05.667 --> 00:08:06.901
"Do it again."
"Yes, ma'am."

00:08:06.901 --> 00:08:08.000
-"Try it again."
-"Yes, ma'am."

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.167
Yeah, that's all we did, yeah.

00:08:09.167 --> 00:08:11.501
-You crushed it.
It's so fun, it's so awesome.

00:08:11.501 --> 00:08:14.000
-We had a ball.
-Get ready to enjoy this.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:15.701
I want to show everyone a clip.
Here's Ryan Reynolds

00:08:15.701 --> 00:08:18.968
and Will Ferrell in "Spirited."
Take a look at this.

00:08:18.968 --> 00:08:21.033
-♪ We're bringing back
Christmas ♪

00:08:21.033 --> 00:08:23.534
♪ We're bringing back
Christmas ♪

00:08:23.534 --> 00:08:25.701
♪ Plus a ton of cash ♪

00:08:25.701 --> 00:08:29.133
♪ From some good
old-fashioned trees ♪

00:08:29.133 --> 00:08:33.100
♪♪

00:08:33.100 --> 00:08:36.367
-♪ Christmas, Christmas ♪

00:08:36.367 --> 00:08:38.434
♪♪

00:08:38.434 --> 00:08:39.634
-Thank you.

00:08:39.634 --> 00:08:47.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:49.534
-Yes!

00:08:49.534 --> 00:08:51.334
-That's our man.

00:08:51.334 --> 00:08:52.734
[ Cheers and applause ]
-That's our man right there.

00:08:52.734 --> 00:08:56.200
Ryan Reynolds!
"Spirited" opens in theaters

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:59.801
this Friday and on Apple TV+
November 18th.

00:08:59.801 --> 00:09:01.968
Jen Psaki joins us
after the break.

00:09:01.968 --> 00:09:03.133
Stick around.

